# 9. Relationship to Other GPL Business Units

## 9.1 Security & Compliance vs Managed Services

Managed Services focuses on the ongoing stability, support, and operational state of the technology environment.

Security & Compliance focuses on how that environment is protected, how access and risk are governed, and whether relevant security requirements are being met.

A Managed Services article may discuss security when it affects infrastructure operations, but if the central argument concerns threat exposure, access governance, vulnerabilities, content protection, or compliance, it likely belongs to Security & Compliance.

## 9.2 Security & Compliance vs Software Services

Software Services focuses on implementing, customizing, integrating, and improving software and workflow systems.

Security & Compliance focuses on the security implications and controls around those systems.

A software integration, automation, internal tool, or production platform can therefore appear in either business unit depending on the question being examined.

If the article asks how the system should function or integrate, it is likely Software Services.

If the article asks what trust, access, exposure, or security risk the system creates, it is likely Security & Compliance.

## 9.3 Security & Compliance vs Consulting

Consulting is primarily strategic and advisory.

Security & Compliance focuses more directly on assessing, implementing, validating, or maintaining security controls and compliance-related requirements.

The distinction may vary by engagement, so articles should avoid forcing a boundary when the subject genuinely involves both.

